.TH PNP-COURIER-SETUP 8 "2026-11-27" "pnp @VERSION@" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
pnp-courier-setup \- prepare a USB stick as a pnp courier stick, self stick or kill card
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sudo pnp-courier-setup
.I DEVICE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Erases the whole USB stick
.I DEVICE
(for example /dev/sdb, not a partition) and makes one GPT partition of pnp's own type, with no filesystem.
Nothing mounts it, and no kernel parses a filesystem someone else's laptop wrote; pnp reads and writes it
directly. The udev rule installed with pnp lets members of the
.B pnp
group use such partitions without root.
.PP
It asks you to type ERASE first, refuses anything that isn't a removable or USB drive, and refuses a drive with
anything mounted. Afterwards, as yourself, run
.B pnp \-\-courier\-check
on the new partition: it writes the whole stick and reads it back, which catches sticks that hold less than they
claim.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pnp (1),
.BR sgdisk (8)
